16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Data</a><a class=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-all text-muted-foreground hover:bg-muted/50 hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/widgets\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-code-xml h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4\"></path><path d=\"m6 8-4 4 4 4\"></path><path d=\"m14.5 4-5 16\"></path></svg>Widgets</a></nav><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/20 hover:shadow-emerald-500/30 transition-all hover:scale-[1.02]\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chart-column h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 3v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16\"></path><path d=\"M18 17V9\"></path><path d=\"M13 17V5\"></path><path d=\"M8 17v-3\"></path></svg>Calculate Now</a><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 shrink-0 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive hover:bg-accent dark:hover:bg-accent/50 h-8 rounded-md gap-1.5 px-3 has-[&gt;svg]:px-2.5 lg:hidden text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\" aria-label=\"Toggle mobile menu\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-menu h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 18h16\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h16\"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id=\"main-content\" class=\"flex-1\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/smartasset-alternative#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"SmartAsset Alternative\",\"item\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/smartasset-alternative\"}]},{\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"@id\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/smartasset-alternative#faq\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is TheTaxCalc really a free SmartAsset alternative?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. TheTaxCalc provides the same core calculators that SmartAsset offers — paycheck calculator, mortgage calculator, retirement calculator, tax refund estimator, and state-by-state comparisons — but every one of our tools is 100% free with no sign-up, no email requirement, and no paywall. We do not require you to create an account, and we never sell your data to financial advisors or third-party lead aggregators.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does TheTaxCalc match leads to financial advisors like SmartAsset does?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. TheTaxCalc does not operate a lead-generation business. When you use a SmartAsset calculator, the company typically asks for your contact information and matches you with up to three financial advisors who pay SmartAsset for those introductions. TheTaxCalc does not collect your income, savings, or contact details, and we never share any user information with third-party financial advisors or brokers.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which calculators does TheTaxCalc offer that compare to SmartAsset?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"TheTaxCalc offers a paycheck calculator for all 50 states, a mortgage calculator with amortization and extra payment support, a 401(k) and retirement projection calculator, a capital gains tax calculator, a self-employment tax calculator, a tax refund estimator, a home sale tax calculator, a bonus tax calculator, an overtime tax calculator, a lottery tax calculator, a sales tax calculator for all 50 states, a property tax calculator, an IRS withholding (W-4) calculator, and a state-by-state comparison tool. All are free, updated for 2026, and run entirely in your browser.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How accurate are TheTaxCalc calculators compared to SmartAsset?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Both TheTaxCalc and SmartAsset use the same primary data sources — IRS Publication 15-T for federal tax withholding, the Social Security Administration for the FICA wage base, and each state's Department of Revenue for state income tax. TheTaxCalc publishes a full methodology page documenting every source, every formula, and every assumption we use, and we update our data within 48 hours of any official IRS or state revenue department change. Our 2026 data is current as of January 2026.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does TheTaxCalc store my salary or financial information?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. All calculations on TheTaxCalc run entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your income, deductions, savings, and tax figures are never transmitted to our servers or stored in any database. We do not require accounts, we do not use tracking cookies on calculator pages, and we cannot tie your calculation results back to you. SmartAsset and many similar lead-generation sites do collect user input — we do not.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I use TheTaxCalc for actual tax filing?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Our calculators are designed for estimation, planning, and education — not for filing your actual tax return. They give you a solid starting point for understanding your take-home pay, refund expectations, and tax planning opportunities. When it's time to actually file, use IRS Free File, commercial tax preparation software, or work with a qualified CPA or Enrolled Agent who understands your full situation. We recommend our paycheck calculator and tax refund calculator as planning tools throughout the year.\"}}]},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"SmartAsset Alternative 2026 — Free Paycheck & Tax Calculators\",\"description\":\"A free, no-sign-up SmartAsset alternative with paycheck, mortgage, retirement, and tax calculators for all 50 states.\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/smartasset-alternative\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"}}]}</script><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span aria-hidden=\"true\">/</span><span class=\"text-foreground font-medium\">SmartAsset Alternative</span></nav><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl mb-4\">The Free SmartAsset Alternative — Paycheck, Mortgage &amp; Tax Calculators</h1><p class=\"text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-8\">SmartAsset built a popular suite of financial calculators — but they also collect your contact information, match you with up to three paying financial advisors, and require an email address before showing you full results. TheTaxCalc is a free, no-strings alternative: every calculator runs in your browser, no sign-up required, and your numbers never touch our servers. Here’s how we compare.</p><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Why Look for a SmartAsset Alternative?</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\">SmartAsset is a well-known personal finance site that publishes a paycheck calculator, a mortgage calculator, a retirement calculator, and several other tools. The site is owned by a company whose business model is lead generation: when you enter your information to use a calculator, SmartAsset typically asks for your name, email, and phone number, then matches you with up to three financial advisors who pay SmartAsset for those introductions.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\">That’s not necessarily a bad thing — many users want advisor introductions. But if you just want to know how much you’ll take home after taxes, or whether you can afford a $400,000 mortgage, you probably don’t want your inbox flooded with advisor solicitations. TheTaxCalc was built to be the no-strings alternative: you type in your numbers, you get your answer, you leave. No accounts, no emails, no advisor matches.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">The other big reason users seek an alternative is privacy. When you enter your salary, savings rate, or mortgage details into a lead-generation calculator, that data is collected, stored, and in some cases shared with third parties. On TheTaxCalc, every calculation runs entirely in your browser using JavaScript — your numbers never reach our servers. We couldn’t see them even if we wanted to.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Feature Comparison</h2><div class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border/30\"><table class=\"w-full text-sm\"><thead class=\"bg-muted/30\"><tr><th class=\"px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold text-foreground\">Feature</th><th class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center font-semibold text-emerald-400\">TheTaxCalc</th><th class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center font-semibold text-muted-foreground\">SmartAsset</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-border/20\"><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Paycheck calculator (50 states)</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Mortgage calculator with amortization</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Retirement / 401(k) calculator</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Capital gains tax calculator</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Self-employment tax calculator</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Bonus, overtime, lottery tax calculators</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">State-by-state comparison tool</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Free with no sign-up</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">No email required to see results</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">No financial advisor lead-matching</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Data never leaves your browser</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">—</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Full published methodology</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr><tr class=\"bg-card/30\"><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-foreground\">Updated for 2026 tax year</td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-emerald-400 font-bold\">✓</span></td><td class=\"px-4 py-3 text-center\"><span class=\"text-muted-foreground\">✓</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class=\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Privacy Is the Difference</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\">The single biggest difference between TheTaxCalc and SmartAsset is what happens to your data. On SmartAsset, when you use the paycheck calculator, you’re prompted to enter your email address to “see your full results.” That email — along with your income, zip code, and filing status — is collected and used to match you with paying financial advisors. The information may also be retained for marketing.</p><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">On TheTaxCalc, the moment you type your salary into the calculator, that number stays in your browser. We don’t have accounts. We don’t collect your email. We don’t have a database of user calculations, because we never receive your calculations in the first place. If you want to share your results, you can copy the URL or screenshot it yourself — but by default, what you calculate on TheTaxCalc is between you and your browser.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">Calculators You Can Use Right Now</h2><div class=\"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2\"><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Paycheck Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Take-home pay for all 50 states with federal, FICA, and state income tax.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/mortgage-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Mortgage Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Monthly payment, amortization schedule, and extra payment scenarios.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/401k-retirement-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">401(k) Retirement Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Project your retirement balance with employer match and compound growth.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/capital-gains-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Capital Gains Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Short-term and long-term capital gains tax with NIIT included.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/self-employment-tax-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Self-Employment Tax Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">SE tax, deduction for employer portion, and quarterly estimates.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/tax-refund-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Tax Refund Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Estimate your federal refund based on withholding and credits.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/home-sale-tax-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Home Sale Tax Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Capital gains on property with $250K/$500K exclusion and depreciation.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\" href=\"/obbba-tax-calculator\"><p class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">OBBBA Tax Calculator</p><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\">Compare your 2026 taxes under the new One Big Beautiful Bill Act.</p></a></div></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\">All 50 States Covered</h2><p class=\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\">TheTaxCalc offers dedicated paycheck calculators for all 50 states. That includes no-income-tax states (Texas, Florida, Washington, Nevada, Wyoming, South Dakota, Alaska, New Hampshire, Tennessee), flat-tax states (Illinois at 4.95%, Pennsylvania at 3.07%, Colorado at 4.4%, Indiana at 3.05%, Michigan at 4.25%, Massachusetts at 5.0%, Georgia at 5.49%, North Carolina at 4.5%), and the most progressive states (California at 1%–13.3%, New York at 4%–10.9% plus NYC tax). Use our<!-- --> <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\" href=\"/paycheck-calculator\">paycheck calculator</a> <!-- -->or compare any two states side-by-side on our<!-- --> <a class=\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\" href=\"/compare\">state comparison page</a>.</p></section><section class=\"mb-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\">SmartAsset Alternative FAQ</h2><div class=\"space-y-4\"><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">Is TheTaxCalc really a free SmartAsset alternative?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Yes. TheTaxCalc provides the same core calculators that SmartAsset offers — paycheck calculator, mortgage calculator, retirement calculator, tax refund estimator, and state-by-state comparisons — but every one of our tools is 100% free with no sign-up, no email requirement, and no paywall. We do not require you to create an account, and we never sell your data to financial advisors or third-party lead aggregators.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">Does TheTaxCalc match leads to financial advisors like SmartAsset does?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">No. TheTaxCalc does not operate a lead-generation business. When you use a SmartAsset calculator, the company typically asks for your contact information and matches you with up to three financial advisors who pay SmartAsset for those introductions. TheTaxCalc does not collect your income, savings, or contact details, and we never share any user information with third-party financial advisors or brokers.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">Which calculators does TheTaxCalc offer that compare to SmartAsset?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">TheTaxCalc offers a paycheck calculator for all 50 states, a mortgage calculator with amortization and extra payment support, a 401(k) and retirement projection calculator, a capital gains tax calculator, a self-employment tax calculator, a tax refund estimator, a home sale tax calculator, a bonus tax calculator, an overtime tax calculator, a lottery tax calculator, a sales tax calculator for all 50 states, a property tax calculator, an IRS withholding (W-4) calculator, and a state-by-state comparison tool. All are free, updated for 2026, and run entirely in your browser.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">How accurate are TheTaxCalc calculators compared to SmartAsset?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Both TheTaxCalc and SmartAsset use the same primary data sources — IRS Publication 15-T for federal tax withholding, the Social Security Administration for the FICA wage base, and each state&#x27;s Department of Revenue for state income tax. TheTaxCalc publishes a full methodology page documenting every source, every formula, and every assumption we use, and we update our data within 48 hours of any official IRS or state revenue department change. Our 2026 data is current as of January 2026.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">Does TheTaxCalc store my salary or financial information?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">No. All calculations on TheTaxCalc run entirely in your browser using JavaScript. Your income, deductions, savings, and tax figures are never transmitted to our servers or stored in any database. We do not require accounts, we do not use tracking cookies on calculator pages, and we cannot tie your calculation results back to you. SmartAsset and many similar lead-generation sites do collect user input — we do not.</p></div><div class=\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\">Can I use TheTaxCalc for actual tax filing?</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">Our calculators are designed for estimation, planning, and education — not for filing your actual tax return. They give you a solid starting point for understanding your take-home pay, refund expectations, and tax planning opportunities. When it&#x27;s time to actually file, use IRS Free File, commercial tax preparation software, or work with a qualified CPA or Enrolled Agent who understands your full situation. We recommend our paycheck calculator and tax refund calculator as planning tools throughout the year.</p></div></div></section><section><div class=\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-muted/10 p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\">TheTaxCalc is an independent personal finance website and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by SmartAsset. SmartAsset is a trademark of its respective owner. All product names, logos, and brands are property of their respective owners. Comparisons on this page are based on publicly available information as of January 2026.</p></div></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><footer class=\"mt-auto border-t border-border/30 glass-strong\"><div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-500/5 via-emerald-500/10 to-emerald-500/5 border-b border-border/20\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\"><div class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-between\"><div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-bold text-foreground\">Stay Updated on <span class=\"text-emerald-400\">Tax Changes</span></h2><p class=\"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Get the latest tax tips, calculator updates, and financial insights delivered to your inbox.</p></div><div class=\"flex w-full max-w-sm gap-2\"><input type=\"email\" data-slot=\"input\" class=\"file:text-foreground selection:bg-primary selection:text-primary-foreground dark:bg-input/30 flex h-9 w-full min-w-0 rounded-md border px-3 py-1 text-base shadow-xs transition-[color,box-shadow] outline-none file:inline-flex file:h-7 file:border-0 file:bg-transparent file:text-sm file:font-medium disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50 md:text-sm focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive bg-background/50 border-border/30 placeholder:text-muted-foreground\" aria-label=\"Email address for newsletter\" placeholder=\"Enter your email\" value=\"\"/><button data-slot=\"button\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-all disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 [&amp;_svg]:pointer-events-none [&amp;_svg:not([class*=&#x27;size-&#x27;])]:size-4 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid: