, North Carolina at 4.5%), and the most progressive states (California at 1%–13.3%, New York at 4%–10.9% plus NYC tax). Use our\\\",\\\" \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L10\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/paycheck-calculator\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"paycheck calculator\\\"}],\\\" \\\",\\\"or compare any two states side-by-side on our\\\",\\\" \\\",[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L10\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/compare\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"state comparison page\\\"}],\\\".\\\"]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"SmartAsset Alternative FAQ\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"Is TheTaxCalc really a free SmartAsset alternative?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Is TheTaxCalc really a free SmartAsset alternative?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Yes. TheTaxCalc provides the same core calculators that SmartAsset offers — paycheck calculator, mortgage calculator, retirement calculator, tax refund estimator, and state-by-state comparisons — but every one of our tools is 100% free with no sign-up, no email requirement, and no paywall. We do not require you to create an account, and we never sell your data to financial advisors or third-party lead aggregators.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"Does TheTaxCalc match leads to financial advisors like SmartAsset does?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Does TheTaxCalc match leads to financial advisors like SmartAsset does?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"No. TheTaxCalc does not operate a lead-generation business. When you use a SmartAsset calculator, the company typically asks for your contact information and matches you with up to three financial advisors who pay SmartAsset for those introductions. TheTaxCalc does not collect your income, savings, or contact details, and we never share any user information with third-party financial advisors or brokers.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"Which calculators does TheTaxCalc offer that compare to SmartAsset?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Which calculators does TheTaxCalc offer that compare to SmartAsset?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"TheTaxCalc offers a paycheck calculator for all 50 states, a mortgage calculator with amortization and extra payment support, a 401(k) and retirement projection calculator, a capital gains tax calculator, a self-employment tax calculator, a tax refund estimator, a home sale tax calculator, a bonus tax calculator, an overtime tax calculator, a lottery tax calculator, a sales tax calculator for all 50 states, a property tax calculator, an IRS withholding (W-4) calculator, and a state-by-state comparison tool. All are free, updated for 2026, and run entirely in your browser.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"How accurate are TheTaxCalc calculators compared to SmartAsset?\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How accurate are TheTaxCalc calculators compared to SmartAsset?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Both TheTaxCalc and SmartAsset use the same primary data sources — IRS Publication 15-T for federal tax withholding, the Social Security Administration for the FICA wage base, and each state's Department of Revenue for state income tax. TheTaxCalc publishes a full methodology page documenting every source, every formula, and every assumption we use, and we update our data within 48 hours of any official IRS or state revenue department change. Our 2026 data is current as of January 2026.\\\"}]]}],\\\"$L2d\\\",\\\"$L2e\\\"]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-muted/10 p-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"TheTaxCalc is an independent personal finance website and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by SmartAsset. SmartAsset is a trademark of its respective owner. All product names, logos, and brands are property of their respective owners. Comparisons on this page are based on publicly available information as of January 2026.\\\"}]}]}]\\n20:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L2f\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$24\\\",null,{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Next.MetadataOutlet\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"$@30\\\"}]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"27:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"—\\\"}]\\n28:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"tr\\\",\\\"No email required to see results\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"b